{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SixOneShapeDiscriminant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SixOneShapeDiscriminant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SixOneShapeDiscriminant.six_one_shape_diff_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SixOneShapeDiscriminant.six_one_shape_diff_sq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SixOneShapeDiscriminant.lean#L59-L73","doc":"**The four 6₁ shape differences square to `257`.** For the four roots of the\n6₁ shape polynomial `x⁴ − 3x³ + 6x² − 5x + 2` (Vieta `Σy = 3`, `Σyᵢyⱼ = 6`,\n`Σyᵢyⱼyₖ = 5`, `∏y = 2`), the product of their squared pairwise differences is the\nfield discriminant `257` — the geometric (shape-difference) form of the 6₁\narithmetic fingerprint, the 6-crossing analogue of `five_two_saddle_diff_sq = −23`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SixOneShapeDiscriminant.disc_eq_root_diff_sq_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SixOneShapeDiscriminant.disc_eq_root_diff_sq_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SixOneShapeDiscriminant.lean#L42-L57","doc":"**Quartic discriminant as the product of squared root differences.** For any\nfour ring elements (the four shapes), the square of the product of their six\npairwise differences equals the quartic discriminant written in the elementary\nsymmetric functions `e₁ = Σyᵢ`, `e₂ = Σyᵢyⱼ`, `e₃ = Σyᵢyⱼyₖ`, `e₄ = ∏yᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}